A||N||1||KissMySSFiero||How long to replace all Ball joints on an 88?||||1||
Z||000000||KissMySSFiero||07-12-2001||04:01 PM||||well its that time.  i have them(about3 months now) and i need to get them done.  im going to have the front cradle down this weekend it looks like.  also ill be replacing all the bushings with poly.  my main concern is time right now.  i dont want to start something thats goin to take too long.  im limited with my time righ tnow because im taking a trip to fla next week.  <BR>how long did it take most of you to replace these?  anyone got any shortcuts or tips for me?  what tools will i need.  just a ball joint press?  im more concerned about removing them.  what do i need for that that i dont have to order?   <BR>TIA<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000001||DRH||07-12-2001||04:21 PM||||I did exactly what you are doing. I don't know the exact hours but it took longer than a weekend. The bushings are going to take longer than just the the ball joints would. The lower control arm bolts will probably be rusted to the inside of the bushing sleeves and be a real "female dog" to get out. It takes a while to get the rubber out of the bushings. I cleaned and painted everything which takes a while also.<P>The ball joints are not a problem. The top one is held in with rivets you drill out. The bottom ones on mine were held in more by rust than anything. I sprayed them with penetrating oil and knocked them out with a hammer. They are "pressed" in, but it's not a real tight fit except for the rust.<P>I don't think I would tackle the whole job with a heavy deadline coming up. You are most likely going to run into some things that will take a while...<P><BR>||||reg||1
